<title>USA: US banks free reserves $1.157 bln Jan 29 two weeks.</title>
<headline>US banks free reserves $1.157 bln Jan 29 two weeks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had  free reserves of $1.157 billion per day in the two weeks ended January 29, versus revised free reserves of $1.175 billion in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $17 million versus $18 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
